{"id":"28f93ddcd4761c3f","group":"58","path":"58/batch05/58-df-operator-norm.md","title":"Operator Norm","display":"df-operator-norm — Operator Norm","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-operator-norm","aliases":["58-df-operator-norm","Operator Norm","58-df-zfc-func-operator-norm"],"display":"df-operator-norm — Operator Norm","depends_on":["[[58-df-normed-space]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-operator-norm"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-operator-norm</span><span>Operator Norm</span><span>58-df-zfc-func-operator-norm</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-operator-norm — Operator Norm"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"bdbbe5a00af04978\" href=\"?note=bdbbe5a00af04978\" title=\"58-df-normed-space\">58-df-normed-space</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r,T,X,Y,K,+_X,+_Y,\\cdot_X,\\cdot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y\\in V\">\\(r,T,X,Y,K,+_X,+_Y,\\cdot_X,\\cdot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y\\in V\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"bdbbe5a00af04978\" href=\"?note=bdbbe5a00af04978\" title=\"58-df-normed-space.md\">58-df-normed-space.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sup_{\\mathbb R}:\\mathcal P(\\mathbb R)\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb R\">\\(\\sup_{\\mathbb R}:\\mathcal P(\\mathbb R)\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb R\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S:V^{11}\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S:V^{11}\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}operator\\text{-}norm}\\vdash\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S(r,T,X,Y,K,+_X,+_Y,\\cdot_X,\\cdot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(X,K,+_X,\\cdot_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_X)\\land\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(Y,K,+_Y,\\cdot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y)\\land T:X\\to Y\\land\\forall x,x&#39;\\in X\\;\\forall\\alpha\\in K\\;\\left(T(x+_Xx&#39;)=T(x)+_YT(x&#39;)\\land T(\\alpha\\cdot_Xx)=\\alpha\\cdot_YT(x)\\right)\\land\\exists C\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\forall x\\in X\\;(\\|T(x)\\|_Y\\leq C\\|x\\|_X)\\land r=\\sup_{\\mathbb R}\\{\\|T(x)\\|_Y:x\\in X\\land\\|x\\|_X\\leq1\\}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}operator\\text{-}norm}\\vdash\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S(r,T,X,Y,K,+_X,+_Y,\\cdot_X,\\cdot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(X,K,+_X,\\cdot_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_X)\\land\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(Y,K,+_Y,\\cdot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y)\\land T:X\\to Y\\land\\forall x,x&#39;\\in X\\;\\forall\\alpha\\in K\\;\\left(T(x+_Xx&#39;)=T(x)+_YT(x&#39;)\\land T(\\alpha\\cdot_Xx)=\\alpha\\cdot_YT(x)\\right)\\land\\exists C\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\forall x\\in X\\;(\\|T(x)\\|_Y\\leq C\\|x\\|_X)\\land r=\\sup_{\\mathbb R}\\{\\|T(x)\\|_Y:x\\in X\\land\\|x\\|_X\\leq1\\}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>When the displayed predicate holds, the unique <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r\">\\(r\\)</span> is written <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|T\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}\">\\(\\|T\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}\\)</span>; it is the least <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"M\">\\(M\\)</span> with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|T(x)\\|_Y\\leq M\\|x\\|_X\">\\(\\|T(x)\\|_Y\\leq M\\|x\\|_X\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>If <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"Y\">\\(Y\\)</span> is Banach, the bounded operators <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X\\to Y\">\\(X\\to Y\\)</span> form a Banach space in this norm.</li>\n<li><code>58-df-zfc-func-operator-norm</code> is merged here.</li>\n<li>Equivalent forms include <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\sup_{\\|x\\|=1}\\|Tx\\|\">\\(\\sup_{\\|x\\|=1}\\|Tx\\|\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\inf\\{M\\mid \\forall x(\\|Tx\\|\\leq M\\|x\\|)\\}\">\\(\\inf\\{M\\mid \\forall x(\\|Tx\\|\\leq M\\|x\\|)\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>For a bounded normal operator, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"r(T)=\\|T\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}=\\max\\{|\\lambda|:\\lambda\\in\\sigma(T)\\}\">\\(r(T)=\\|T\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}=\\max\\{|\\lambda|:\\lambda\\in\\sigma(T)\\}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Nuclear norm: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|T\\|_1 = \\sum_n s_n(T)\">\\(\\|T\\|_1 = \\sum_n s_n(T)\\)</span>; trace class</li>\n<li>Hilbert-Schmidt: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\|T\\|_2^2 = \\sum_n s_n(T)^2 = \\mathrm{tr}(T^*T)\">\\(\\|T\\|_2^2 = \\sum_n s_n(T)^2 = \\mathrm{tr}(T^*T)\\)</span></li>\n<li>On an operator space, the norm topology is stronger than the strong-operator topology, which is stronger than the weak-operator topology.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Reference\">[Reference]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Reed and Simon, Methods of Mathematical Physics Vol. 1</li>\n<li>Conway, A Course in Functional Analysis</li>\n<li>Simon, Trace Ideals and Their Applications</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2},{"id":"Reference","text":"[Reference]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-normed-space","status":"resolved","id":"bdbbe5a00af04978","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-normed-space]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-normed-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"bdbbe5a00af04978","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}$ (see [[58-df-normed-space.md]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"r,T,X,Y,K,+_X,+_Y,\\cdot_X,\\cdot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S:V^5\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\sup_{\\mathbb R}:\\mathcal P(\\mathbb R)\\rightharpoonup\\mathbb R","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S:V^{11}\\to\\{\\top,\\bot\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}operator\\text{-}norm}\\vdash\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S(r,T,X,Y,K,+_X,+_Y,\\cdot_X,\\cdot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y)\\leftrightarrow\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(X,K,+_X,\\cdot_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_X)\\land\\mathrm{NormedSpace}_S(Y,K,+_Y,\\cdot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y)\\land T:X\\to Y\\land\\forall x,x'\\in X\\;\\forall\\alpha\\in K\\;\\left(T(x+_Xx')=T(x)+_YT(x')\\land T(\\alpha\\cdot_Xx)=\\alpha\\cdot_YT(x)\\right)\\land\\exists C\\in\\mathbb R_{\\geq0}\\;\\forall x\\in X\\;(\\|T(x)\\|_Y\\leq C\\|x\\|_X)\\land r=\\sup_{\\mathbb R}\\{\\|T(x)\\|_Y:x\\in X\\land\\|x\\|_X\\leq1\\}","display":true},{"tex":"r","display":false},{"tex":"\\|T\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}","display":false},{"tex":"M","display":false},{"tex":"\\|T(x)\\|_Y\\leq M\\|x\\|_X","display":false},{"tex":"Y","display":false},{"tex":"X\\to Y","display":false},{"tex":"\\sup_{\\|x\\|=1}\\|Tx\\|","display":false},{"tex":"\\inf\\{M\\mid \\forall x(\\|Tx\\|\\leq M\\|x\\|)\\}","display":false},{"tex":"r(T)=\\|T\\|_{\\mathrm{op}}=\\max\\{|\\lambda|:\\lambda\\in\\sigma(T)\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\|T\\|_1 = \\sum_n s_n(T)","display":false},{"tex":"\\|T\\|_2^2 = \\sum_n s_n(T)^2 = \\mathrm{tr}(T^*T)","display":false}],"bytes":2054,"backlinks":[{"id":"c740b73b26d2ecf9","anchor":"ref-3","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"dfd5be6f22b3deb4","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"$\\mathrm{OperatorNorm}_S$ (operator-norm value predicate, see [[58-df-operator-norm]])"},{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-908","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-operator-norm.md|58-df-operator-norm]]（batch05）"}],"outgoing":["bdbbe5a00af04978"]}